"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[4482],{78051:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"_connectOccupantSignal","desc":"Bridges a vehicle\'s `occupiedSignal` to the driver\'s client. On\\n`StartControl` it dispatches `VEHICLE_START_CONTROL` with `active = true` and\\nsets the character\'s `InVehicle` attribute; on `StopControl` it does the\\nreverse.\\n\\nThe dispatch is targeted at the occupant only \u2014 other clients neither need nor\\nget it, since they do not simulate the vehicle.","params":[{"name":"vehicle","desc":"The freshly spawned vehicle","lua_type":"Vehicle.Vehicle"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":80,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"init","desc":"Bootstrap hook. Registers the `Handlers` folder with `red`, which is what\\nmakes `VEHICLE_SPAWN`, `VEHICLE_DESPAWN` and `VEHICLE_LOG_DISTANCE` reachable\\nfrom clients.\\n\\nNo-ops entirely when the `Vehicle` feature flag is off \u2014 with it disabled\\nthere is no client-reachable surface at all.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":115,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"start","desc":"Bootstrap hook. Despawns a leaving player\'s vehicle and clears their debounce,\\nso a car cannot outlive its owner.\\n\\nNo-ops entirely when the `Vehicle` feature flag is off.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":132,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"spawnVehicle","desc":"Spawns a vehicle for `player` and returns its model, or `nil` if it could not\\nbe placed.\\n\\nRefused outright in the lobby (`PlaceUtility.isLobby`) and while the player\'s\\none-second debounce is active. Any existing vehicle is despawned first, which\\nis what enforces one vehicle per player \u2014 this is a *replace*, not an add.\\n\\nPlacement itself is decided by [Vehicle.new], which re-runs the same ground\\nand clearance checks the client did before asking; a `nil` from there means no\\nlegal spot and is returned as-is.\\n\\nOn success it starts the vehicle\'s idle despawn timer, wires the occupancy\\nbridge, records an analytics event, and fires `VehicleSpawned`.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"Owner of the new vehicle","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The spawned car, or nil","lua_type":"Model?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":165,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"despawnVehicle","desc":"Removes the player\'s vehicle and fires `VehicleDespawned`. No-ops if they have\\nnone.\\n\\nPrefers the [Vehicle] wrapper\'s `Destroy` so the despawn timer is cancelled\\nand seated characters have their collision restored; falls back to destroying\\nthe bare model if the wrapper is somehow missing from the cache.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":219,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"getPlayerVehicle","desc":"Returns the player\'s current vehicle model, or `nil`.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Model?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":247,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"getAttachmentConfig","desc":"Looks up an attachment\'s config (its slot type and model) in\\n`VehicleAttachmentData`. Returns `nil` for an unknown name.","params":[{"name":"attachmentName","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"VehicleAttachmentData.AttachmentConfig?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":261,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"equipAttachment","desc":"Equips an attachment onto the player\'s vehicle.\\n\\nSlots hold one attachment each: whatever currently occupies\\n`config.attachmentType` is removed first, so equipping is idempotent and\\nswapping needs no explicit unequip.\\n\\nReturns `false` for an unknown attachment name, a player with no vehicle, or a\\nfailed attach (bad slot, model without a PrimaryPart).","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"attachmentName","desc":"Key into `VehicleAttachmentData`","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Whether the attachment is now equipped","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":284,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"unequipAttachment","desc":"Removes whatever is in the given slot on the player\'s vehicle.\\n\\nNote this takes a **slot type**, not an attachment name \u2014 the same key\\n[VehicleService.equipAttachment] derives from the config.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"attachmentType","desc":"Slot to clear","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Whether something was removed","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":326,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"getAttachmentAtSlot","desc":"Returns the attachment model in the given slot on the player\'s vehicle, or\\n`nil`.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"attachmentSlot","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Model?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":353,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"getAllAttachments","desc":"Returns the player\'s vehicle\'s whole slot-to-model attachment map, or `nil` if\\nthey have no vehicle.\\n\\nThe returned table is the vehicle\'s live map, not a copy.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"{ [string]: Model }?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":384,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"setSpeedMultiplier","desc":"Scales the player\'s vehicle\'s top speed. The value is written to the car\'s\\n`SpeedMultiplier` attribute and read by the driving client each frame, so it\\ntakes effect immediately without a remote.\\n\\nClamped to 0..1 by [Vehicle:SetSpeedMultiplier] \u2014 this can only ever slow a\\nvehicle down, and 0 is a full stop.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"multiplier","desc":"0..1","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":414,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"brake","desc":"Cuts the player\'s vehicle to zero speed by setting its multiplier to 0. The\\nmultiplier stays at 0 until something raises it \u2014 taking the driver\'s seat\\nresets it to 1.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":440,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"ejectDriver","desc":"Forcibly removes the driver from the player\'s vehicle, placing them on the\\nground beside it.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"Owner of the vehicle, not necessarily the driver","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":465,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"ejectPassenger","desc":"Forcibly removes the passenger from the player\'s vehicle.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"Owner of the vehicle","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":489,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"ejectAll","desc":"Empties the player\'s vehicle \u2014 driver and passenger both.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"Owner of the vehicle","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":513,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"ejectPlayer","desc":"Ejects one specific occupant from a vehicle, whichever seat they are in.\\nNo-ops if the target is not aboard.","params":[{"name":"vehicleOwner","desc":"Whose vehicle to act on","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"targetPlayer","desc":"The occupant to remove","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":539,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}},{"name":"logDistanceDriven","desc":"Credits distance driven to the player\'s profile and records it in analytics.\\n\\nCalled from the `VEHICLE_LOG_DISTANCE` handler when a driver dismounts, so the\\nvalue originates on the client. It is capped at what a car could cover since\\nthe last credit (or the player\'s first spawn); a player who never spawned a\\nvehicle this session is credited nothing.\\n\\n`ProfileService` is required lazily inside the function to avoid a\\nrequire-time cycle between the two services.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"distance","desc":"Studs travelled this session","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":572,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"VehicleService","desc":"Handles vehicle spawning, despawning, and player lifecycle.\\n\\n### Responsibilities\\n\\nThis service owns the **one vehicle per player** invariant and is the entry\\npoint every other server system uses. It holds a `player \u2192 car Model` map and\\ndelegates all per-vehicle behaviour to a [Vehicle] instance looked up from that\\nmodel via `Vehicle.getCar`. That indirection is why nearly every method here is\\nthe same three-step shape: resolve the player\'s car, resolve its Vehicle\\nwrapper, forward the call.\\n\\nPhysics lives on the driver\'s client (see [VehicleController]); this side owns\\nexistence, seat authority, attachments and stats.\\n\\n### Occupancy bridge\\n\\n[VehicleService._connectOccupantSignal] is the seam between the two realms. A\\n[Vehicle] fires `occupiedSignal` when someone takes or leaves the driver\'s\\nseat; this service turns that into a `VEHICLE_START_CONTROL` dispatch to that\\nclient (which starts or stops its physics loop) and mirrors the state onto the\\ncharacter\'s `InVehicle` attribute so other systems can read it without asking.\\n\\nGated by [FeatureFlags].Vehicle \u2014 disabled by default; per-project forks enable\\nit deliberately. With the flag off neither `init` nor `start` runs, so the\\nremote handlers are never registered and no vehicle can be spawned from the\\nclient \u2014 but the direct API below is still callable by server code.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/survival-islands - proprietary and confidential.","tags":["dormant"],"realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":36,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/VehicleService.luau"}}')}}]);